{"name":"Mesa Beige","hex":"#f2ebd6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mesa","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flat area of land higher than other land, with one or more clifflike edges.","a structure with components rising above the insulating substrate that surrounds it"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mesa"},{"term":"beige","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour, variously defined from a pale brown, to a yellow greyish off-white.","Debeige; a kind of woollen or mixed dress goods."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a slightly yellowish gray colour, as that of unbleached wool.","Comfortably dull and unadventurous, in a way that suggests middle-class suburbia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beige"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mesa","blocks":[{"text":"A mesa is an isolated, flat-topped elevation, ridge, or hill, bounded from all sides by steep escarpments and standing distinctly above a surrounding plain. Mesas consist of flat-lying soft sedimentary rocks, such as shales, capped by a resistant layer of harder rock, like sandstone or limestone, forming a caprock that protects the flat summit. The caprock may also include dissected lava flows or eroded duricrust."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Over_Monument_Valley%2C_Navajo_Nation.jpg/330px-Over_Monument_Valley%2C_Navajo_Nation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesa","wikidata":"Q623319"},{"title":"Beige","blocks":[{"text":"Beige is variously described as a pale sandy fawn color, a grayish tan, a light-grayish yellowish brown, or a pale to grayish yellow. It takes its name from French, where the word originally meant natural wool that has been neither bleached nor dyed, hence also the color of natural wool."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Saint_Anthony_church_in_Chamboret_07.jpg/330px-Saint_Anthony_church_in_Chamboret_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beige","wikidata":"Q843607"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/HarQatum.jpg/500px-HarQatum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/HarQatum.jpg/1280px-HarQatum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/HarQatum.jpg/500px-HarQatum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Har Qatum, a mesa located on the southern edge of Makhtesh Ramon, Israel","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHarQatum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Ingleborough_from_Little_Ingleborough_-_geograph.org.uk_-_548604.jpg/500px-Ingleborough_from_Little_Ingleborough_-_geograph.org.uk_-_548604.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Ingleborough_from_Little_Ingleborough_-_geograph.org.uk_-_548604.jpg/500px-Ingleborough_from_Little_Ingleborough_-_geograph.org.uk_-_548604.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ingleborough in North Yorkshire, England","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIngleborough_from_Little_Ingleborough_-_geograph.org.uk_-_548604.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Mesa_in_Colorado.jpg/500px-Mesa_in_Colorado.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Mesa_in_Colorado.jpg/1280px-Mesa_in_Colorado.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb